{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi7fGQyv6eVbYh6aPmRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The list page now renders the labels from state as a keyed list of badges, with an \"Add a label\" button and a \"Remove\" button on each item. `npm run test:hydration` (113 passed), `npm run test:e2e` (11 passed) and `npm test` (278 passed) all pass. Everything is committed in `4468c56`.\n\nHow it works, in `example-hydration/pages/list.ts`: the list is a reactive region that maps the labels to `<li key=label>` items. Each item holds a badge and a remove button that calls `State.removeLabel`. The add button calls `State.addLabel` with a label that isn't already in the list.\n\nTests added first, and both failed before the page change:\n- **`test/hydration.ts`:** the `/list` response has exactly one keyed `<li>` per label in the state script, in the same order.\n- **`test/e2e/hydration.spec.ts`:** counts the server's badges with JavaScript blocked, then loads the page normally and checks:\n  - the count is unchanged after the client entry runs;\n  - adding a label adds one badge and removing one takes one away;\n  - the removed item's key is gone;\n  - the first badge is the same element throughout;\n  - the runtime assertions contain no FAIL.\n\n`npm run lint` reports two errors, both unused variables in `test/plugins.ts`. They were there before this ticket and I didn't touch that file. I also added a short note to `AGENTS.md` on the keyed-list pattern and the Playwright trick for counting server-rendered hosts.\n\n[x] The list route's server response has one keyed item per label in the state script\n[x] Adding a label increases the number of badge hosts by one\n[x] Removing a label decreases the number of badge hosts by one, and the removed item's key is gone\n[x] A badge host that was present before an add or remove is the same element afterwards (identity check via an element handle)\n[x] Loading the page adopts the server's badges: the host count is the same before and after the client entry runs\n[x] The runtime assertions contain no FAIL\n[x] `npm run test:hydration` and `npm run test:e2e` pass"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":503,"cache_read_input_tokens":60680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":503},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4284ce4b-9585-4f9a-99cb-5fc3d46e0142","uuid":"936e6627-dd6c-4da8-b3cb-6050dc1b9ce8","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:07:13.650Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi7fEXP1kBRanCGfjtHk"}
